Z||000000||Sunnbeam||04-03-2001||11:23 AM||||(A) How do I remove the headlight motor without breaking anything?<P>(B) What parts do I need to rebuild the motor?  I get conflicting info from local sources, i.e. metal gear vs. plastic gear, etc.  <BR>THANX<P>George <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||jaguiler||04-03-2001||12:22 PM||||Ok I had a prob with my pass. side headlight motor too on my 86 GT.  I tried replacing the plastic gear last weekend,  my wife was not happy with me at the time for spending so much time on my car.  It is my daily driver so it has to be perfect for me.... oh well.... anyway her not being happy I could not concentrate on my headlight repair.  I muffed it up.  So it is not the easiest thing to do either.  <BR>I went on ebay and found this guy, David Solt, "solt@rsn.hp.com", who was selling 2 motors rebuilt for $75.00 - (buy it now) <BR>I think this is a pretty good deal and you can replace both at the same time!  At this price it is not worth the time for us to rebuild them.  I would not trust junk yard parts or "used" unrebuilt parts at all.  You never know when they will go out. <BR>My 2 sense worth<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||209.246.221.125||reg||10
Z||000002||jaguiler||04-03-2001||12:24 PM||||By the way.... I forgot to mention, it seems like he makes a small business out of rebuilding these motors for us.  Nice guy too.... will give small amount of cash for your old motors.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||209.246.221.125||reg||14
