Z||000004||mrfixit58||04-03-2001||02:47 PM||||I can't help you on the "86" part because I own an 87. But, the easiest way to remove the motor is to remove the whole headlight assembly. First, Unplug the headlight and the door motor. Raise you headlight (if you can) by cranking the knob. Use a 10mm socket and a 4' to 6' extension ( I like to use 1/4 drive for this). Loosen the nuts located at the bottom corners of the frames (It's not necessary to remove them). Remove the two top 10mm nuts. Push the frame forward until it clears the top studs and lift. That's all there is to it. Reverse order to reinstall.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
